<title>CANADA: Alberta Wheat Pool sees drought stress on crops.</title>
<headline>Alberta Wheat Pool sees drought stress on crops.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberta Wheat Pool on Friday lowered slightly  its crop condition rating as of July 28 from July 21 conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;Areas of eastern Alberta are showing signs of crop stress due to  a lack of moisture,&quot; AWP report said.</p>
<p>&quot;Many stations report barley crops are deteriorating due to high temperatures  and a lack of moisture. In some areas of the southern regions even  a rain now may not benefit these crops,&quot; AWP added. &quot;Warm, sunny weather  is still required in the Peace district to allow crops to use available  moisture.&quot;  </p>
<p>AWP crop condition index of 100 represents optimal growing conditions  while 50 represents average crop output.</p>
